comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z",claude,Verified by pinning sha2 to 0.11.0 locally and running the full suite before committing the bump
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z",claude,The golden hash in tests create_contract.rs is what makes this upgrade safe to prove rather than assume
  "2026-08-10T06:40:18.241Z",claude,"just release-check passes end to end on this branch: cargo fmt check, clippy with all and pedantic denied plus unwrap expect and panic denied, the docstring gate, all 41 tests, coverage at 100 percent across lines functions regions and branches, cargo audit over 95 crate dependencies with no advisories, and the timezone stable changelog check."
  "2026-08-10T06:40:18.953Z",claude,"The encoding was proved byte identical rather than assumed. The full suite was run twice, once with sha2 pinned to 0.10.9 and once with 0.11.0, with the committed golden hash 6eb97257a863250fafbcc2d460f0b9a08a1b864bebf2c725632258e3f72db01c unchanged in both. That assertion is the oracle, so it was deliberately not touched."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:45:39.847Z",claude,A formatting shorthand can be a hidden dependency on a transitive type. The LowerHex implementation belonged to generic-array rather than to sha2 so nothing in the call site named the crate that made it compile
