close_reason: The nibble encoding compiles against both sha2 releases and the golden hash proves it byte identical
body: "Dependabot pull request 8 bumped sha2 from 0.10.9 to 0.11.0 and every platform job failed with E0277, the trait bound Array LowerHex is not satisfied. The digest was rendered with the format shorthand, which resolves through the LowerHex implementation that generic-array provides. sha2 0.11 returns hybrid-array Array instead and that type deliberately does not implement LowerHex. Encoding one byte at a time depends only on u8 and so compiles against both releases. The encoding is byte identical, which the committed golden hash proves."
